Rem ==================================================================
Rem spiro-anim.shoddy — the same drawing, watched.
Rem
Rem Run: mill run spiro-anim.shoddy   (or open it and press Ctrl+R)
Rem
Rem An optional extra, not part of the tutorial's path. spiro.shoddy
Rem folds the whole plan and blits once, so the picture arrives all at
Rem at once; this one blits after every step and pauses a moment, so you
Rem can watch the spiral wind itself outward line by line. It is worth
Rem running once just to see what the Fold in spiro.shoddy is doing.
Rem
Rem It also draws on the documentation's own icon background rather than
Rem black, because the animated icon on the tutorials page is a
Rem recording of this program.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "turtle.shoddy"
Include "spiro-core.shoddy"

Rem Steps to draw here — fewer than the finished picture, so the spiral
Rem fills a small frame instead of running off the edges.
Def IconSteps() As Number
    80

Rem The turtle's surface is a scribbler, and a scribbler is the one
Rem thing in Shoddy that is mutated in place — filling it repaints the
Rem background under everything drawn later. #171a20 is the colour every
Rem icon in the documentation sits on.
Def IconBackground(t As Turtle) As Turtle
    Let filled = ScribblerFill(Sc(t), 23, 26, 32)
    t

Rem One step, then show it: the only difference from spiro.shoddy's Draw.
Def DrawSlowly(t As Turtle, s As Step) As Turtle
    Let inked = SetPenColor(t, Red(s), Green(s), Blue(s))
    Let moved = TurnRight(Forward(inked, Ahead(s)), Turn(s))
    Let shown = Blit(moved)
    Sleep(40)
    moved

Def Main()
    Let start = IconBackground(Title(NewTurtle(480, 300), "Shoddy Spirograph"))
    Let drawn = Fold(Plan(IconSteps()), start, DrawSlowly)
    Let held = Blit(drawn)
    Sleep(1500)
    Print("drew " & Str(IconSteps()) & " steps")
